        "segment_id": "iron-snail:nM_g-z5zLJ0:s0003",
        "note": "Corrects the earlier claim (segment 2) that the 1960s arcuate looked hand-stitched: all of them were done by machine, and Levi's probably changed the pattern over time."
      },
      {
        "segment_id": "iron-snail:nM_g-z5zLJ0:s0010",
        "note": "Corrects the earlier claim (segment 10) that the vintage back-pocket bartack skipped a layer because machines couldn't sew through all the denim: since the belt loops are bartacked all the way through, Levi's more likely hid the bartack for style, though it is less durable."
      }
